From e8e8a28974447a43a991f41196aecc7289d5c6f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jorink <maxjorink@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:26:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] bar-tooltips: show a tooltip when hovering a status
 segment

The status line may carry segment markers and tooltip texts:
  seg0 \x1f seg1 \x1f ... \x1e tip0 \x1f tip1 ...
The markers are removed before drawing. While drawing the status,
drawbar() records where each segment starts; when the pointer is over
the status part of the bar, the tooltip of that segment is drawn in a
scene buffer on the overlay layer, under (or above) the bar, and is
refreshed with every new status line while it is shown. Without the
pointer over the bar this costs one rectangle test per motion event.
Status lines without markers behave as before.

The status text buffer grows to 512 bytes (1024 read per line).
---
 dwl.c | 134 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 131 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

